ling visibility"], "rationale": "The fundamentals point to a Democratic hold: a D+2 open seat, a pro-Democratic environment, and heavy outside spending backing Shaheen, while markets and most raters call it Likely or Solid D. The lone UNH poll showing a narrower +4 and two Lean D ratings justify trimming the expected margin to around 8 points rather than the full fundamentals-based figure.", "watch": "A late surge of Republican outside money or a second poll confirming a single-digit race would move this toward Lean D.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Chris Pappas (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Chris Pappas's run for Senate leaves New Hampshire's first district open, and Democrats have turned to Stefany Shaheen while Republicans nominated Anthony DiLorenzo. The district leans Democratic by about two points, and the 2026 environment favors Democrats, giving the party a structural edge even without an incumbent on the ballot.\n\nShaheen holds a cash-on-hand advantage and benefits from roughly $2.2 million in outside support, while DiLorenzo has raised competitively but spent heavily in the primary. The only public poll, from the University of New Hampshire, showed Shaheen up four points among likely voters. Most expert raters call the race Likely D, with a couple at Lean D, and prediction markets price a Democratic win around 95%. National Democratic leaders have campaigned here, underscoring the seat's role in House control.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.937, "margin": 10.01}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9238, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9245, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.8928, "margin": 7.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.8695, "margin": 7.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.844, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.871, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.8487, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.8802, "margin": 7.0}, {"date":